es among monetary ones; judge by title."},{"publisher":"NBER","role":"signal","window_hours":168,"feeds":[{"name":"New working papers","url":"https://back.nber.org/rss/new.xml"}],"note":"Working papers on climate damages and adaptation economics appear weekly among all fields; judge by title. The feed carries no dates, so treat every item as inside the window and rely on the archive check for repeats."},{"publisher":"Climate Policy Initiative","role":"signal","window_hours":168,"feeds":[{"name":"All","url":"https://www.climatepolicyinitiative.org/feed/"}]},{"publisher":"Nature","role":"signal","window_hours":168,"feeds":[{"name":"Nature Climate Change","url":"https://www.nature.com/nclimate.rss"},{"name":"Nature Water","url":"https://www.nature.com/natwater.rss"},{"name":"Nature Sustainability","url":"https://www.nature.com/natsustain.rss"},{"name":"Nature Reviews Earth and Environment","url":"https://www.nature.com/natrevearthenviron.rss"}],"note":"The projection journals. nature.com has challenged the page tool on some days and read on others; when unreadable, run from the abstract in the feed."},{"publisher":"The Conversation","role":"signal","window_hours":72,"feeds":[{"name":"Environment (US)","url":"https://theconversation.com/us/environment/articles.atom"}],"note":"Researchers writing up their own projections; readable."},{"publisher":"European Environment Agency","role":"signal","window_hours":168,"feeds":[{"name":"News","url":"https://www.eea.europa.eu/en/newsroom/news/rss.xml"}]}],"coverage":{"search":"unconstrained","prefer":["complete","authoritative","accessible"],"mark_subscriber_links":true,"discovery_per_subtopic":false,"discovery_note":"No web-search discovery, as in the general topic. Google News search feeds for restrictions and insurance were tested and left out at launch because their links cannot be read; see the source research."},"editorial":{"two_axes":true,"summary_length":"2 to 4 sentences","summary_rule":"original prose, written from coverage the agent read; no verbatim passages beyond a short attributed quote. Where a story carries a number (a toll, a loss estimate, an allocation, a projected change), the number and its source are the point; keep them.","mark_thin_summaries":true},"evolution":{"mode":"propose"},"subtopic_scope_notes":{"weather-volatility":"Storms, heat, cold, flood, fire, and the swings between them, worldwide, with their tolls and records; and the projections: attribution studies, seasonal outlooks, the monthly climate reports, changes in frequency and intensity. The agencies that publish the outlooks (NOAA, Copernicus, the WMO) have no feeds, so their reports arrive through the desks that cover them.","water":"Restrictions, rationing, allocations, shortages, aquifer and reservoir levels, snowpack, and the litigation and agreements that divide water, worldwide with the U.S. West in depth because that is where the reporting is; and the projections: basin forecasts, groundwater studies, availability under warming. A restriction or allocation decision outranks a report about one.","economics":"What physical risk costs and who pays: insured and uninsured losses, insurer withdrawals and rate actions, reinsurance pricing and catastrophe bonds, crop and commodity effects, municipal and sovereign exposure; and the projections: catastrophe models, central-bank and research-institute work, loss reports from the reinsurers. Energy-transition finance is out of scope unless it prices physical risk."},"source_roles":{"agenda":"Sets what is significant today. Seven desks: the Guardian''s extreme weather, climate crisis and water feeds; NYT Climate; Carbon Brief; Circle of Blue; Artemis; Insurance Journal; FT Climate Capital.","signal":"Corroborates and widens the aperture, and carries the projections: the attribution and research sources, the regional water press, the reinsurance trade press. Items are candidates like any other, judged on consequence; a story only these feeds surfaced is the mea